{
  "slug": "harness-engineering",
  "name": "Harness Engineering",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "AI Agent Harness Engineering: bootstrap, audit, and evolve a reliable 6-layer agent harness for any project. Generates AGENTS.md, hooks (type-check, .env protection, auto-format), architecture docs, and sprint planning tools. Supports Claude Code and CodeBuddy. Works with TypeScript, Python, Go, Java, and generic stacks.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **19 skills**, **4 agents**, **10 commands** and **4 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (19): `archive`, `audit` (Health check and optimization for existing project Harness setups), `brainstorming` (You MUST use this before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality, or modifying behavior), `canary`, `dispatching-parallel-agents` (Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies), `evolve` (Continuous iteration and evolution of the Harness framework), `executing-plans` (Use when you have a written implementation plan to execute in a separate session with review checkpoints), `finishing-a-development-branch` (Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and you need to decide how to integrate the work…), and 11 more\n- **Agents** (4): `code-review-agent` (Code quality Inferential Sensor), `coding-agent` (Long-cycle multi-session coding tasks), `explore-agent` (Lightweight codebase exploration), `security-reviewer` (Professional security code review)\n- **Commands** (10): `assign` (Sprint feature assignment planner), `audit` (Perform a health audit on the current project's Harness system, generating a score report and optimization recommendations), `canary` (Generate a canary deployment runbook with risk assessment, staged rollout plan, rollback triggers, and observability checklists), `dump` (Save key decisions and progress from the current session to documentation, for cross-session handoff of long tasks), `init` (Initialize the full AI Agent Harness engineering system for the current project), `review-pr` (PR code review — thin wrapper over harness:requesting-code-review + harness:receiving-code-review), `scan-arch` (Run an architecture health scan to check for dependency violations, oversized modules, and missing tests), `scan-entropy` (Detect codebase entropy — find dead code, duplicate implementations, and excessive coupling, then generate a health report), and 2 more\n- **Hooks** (4): `SessionStart`, `Stop`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install harness-engineering@claude-community` from `huangbaixun/harness-engineering`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 19,
    "agent": 4,
    "hook": 4,
    "command": 10
  },
